    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0052",
      "sequence": 64,
      "meaning": "Śiva tells Satī that, if her doubt is so strong, she may go test Rāma while he waits beneath the banyan until she returns; she should use discernment to dispel her heavy delusion. With his permission she leaves, wondering what to do. Śiva foresees no good for Dakṣa’s daughter: even his counsel has not removed her doubt, and when fate turns adverse well-being is impossible. Saying that only what Rāma has ordained will occur and that argument merely multiplies branches, he repeats Hari’s name. Satī approaches the abode of bliss, repeatedly reflects, assumes Sītā’s form, and walks ahead on the road by which the royal prince is coming.",
