    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0054",
      "sequence": 66,
      "meaning": "Satī reproaches herself for rejecting Śaṅkara’s counsel and projecting her ignorance onto Rāma; she burns inwardly, unsure what answer she can give. Knowing her pain, Rāma reveals a portion of his power. As she travels, Satī beholds a wonder: Rāma and his noble brother appear ahead; looking back, she sees the Lord with his brother and Sītā in their beautiful forms. Wherever she looks, the Lord is seated and served by accomplished sages. She sees countless Śivas, Brahmās and Viṣṇus, each possessing immeasurable power, and all the gods in varied forms bowing at his feet. She also sees innumerable Satīs, creator-goddesses and Lakṣmīs, each embodied in a form corresponding to that of Brahmā and the other gods.",
