    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0055",
      "sequence": 67,
      "meaning": "Wherever Satī looks, she sees as many Raghupatis as there are gods, each accompanied by his powers, and every kind of moving and unmoving creature in the universe. Gods in many guises worship the Lord, but she sees no form of Rāma other than the one before her. Amid the many Raghupatis she sees no many forms of Sītā: it is always the same Raghubara, Lakṣmaṇa and Sītā. Terrified, trembling and bereft of bodily awareness, she closes her eyes and sits on the road. When Dakṣa’s daughter opens them again, nothing remains. Bowing her head repeatedly at Rāma’s feet, she returns to Giriśa. As she approaches, Maheśa smiles, asks after her welfare, and requests the full truth of how she conducted the test.",
